<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Portuguese Bahrain</h1><p class="st-meta">1521 CE – 1602 CE · capital Bahrain Fort</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Bahrain under Portuguese overlordship, ruled through Hormuz from a rebuilt fort, until Safavid Persia took the island in 1602.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1521 a Portuguese and Hormuzi force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-correia">Antonio Correia</a> attacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a>, defeating and fatally wounding the Jabrid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muqrin-ibn-zamil">Muqrin ibn Zamil</a>. The islands passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ormus">Kingdom of Ormus</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> was governed by Hormuzi governors, while the Portuguese kept a garrison and rebuilt the fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qalat-al-bahrain">Qal'at al-Bahrain</a>. The islands' value lay in their pearls and dates and in their position. Local revolts broke out, notably in 1529, and an Ottoman attempt to take the island in 1559 failed. The Portuguese presence itself was small for most of the period.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1602 the local governor was overthrown and the Safavid governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, which held it for most of the next 120 years. The fort, now part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">World Heritage Site</a>, is the main relic.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1521 CE – 1602 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="s